    "https://www.msmu.edu/student-life/career--professional-development/": {
      "title": "Career & Professional Development",
      "description": "Career & Professional Development - MSMU Skip Main Navigation Skip to site alert Directory myMSMU Search Submit MSMU MSMU Meet the Mount Degrees & Programs Admission & Aid Apply Info Give Menu Home / Student Life / Career & Professional Development Career & Professional Development Skip Sub Navigation Explore This Section Close Login to Handshake CPD on myMSMU Find lifelong career success with Mount Saint Mary’s University At Career & Professional Development (CPD), we believe career growth is a cornerstone of leadership development. Our team is passionate about helping students find work that is meaningful to them and aligns with their passions, talents and goals — work that creates a positive impact in the world. With programs and services available at both the Chalon and Doheny campuses, CPD offers personalized career coaching, engaging workshops and connections with recruiters and industry professionals. Unlike most universities, CPD provides career coaching for up to five years after graduation, ensuring students are supported well beyond their time at the Mount. Career services for students and recent alumni We offer a comprehensive suite of services to empower students and recent alumni in building meaningful and impactful careers. From personalized career exploration and job search strategies to hands-on interview practice and networking guidance, we’re here to support your unique goals every step of the way. Career exploration Discover careers that match your passions and strengths. Learn how to align your skills with exciting job opportunities and master the building blocks of the job search process to achieve your goals. Job and internship search Let us help you find your next big opportunity. Get expert advice tailored to your unique interests and goals, with strategies to land the perfect job or internship for your future. Cover letter writing Make your application stand out — work one-on-one with our advisors to craft compelling cover letters that highlight your qualifications and leave a lasting impression on potential employers. Resume building With comprehensive support for crafting, refining and optimizing your resume, our advisors help you showcase your individual strengths and experiences to employers and graduate programs. Graduate school preparation Get personalized guidance on choosing graduate programs, writing personal statements, securing recommendations and navigating the application process with ease. Interview preparation Work with an advisor to learn expert techniques, common questions and strategies to present your best self with confidence. For students and alumni looking to practice their interview skills, we suggest scheduling a mock interview. Mock interview and practice Engage in a simulated interview tailored to your field of interest and receive personalized feedback to impress employers and graduate school admission teams. This hands-on practice helps students and alumni refine their skills, build confidence and effectively prepare for job, internship and graduate school interviews. Networking and outreach skills Learn how to make meaningful professional connections, leverage social media, reach out to people for informational interviews and shine at industry events with tips and strategies from our advisors. Offer evaluation and negotiation Advisors can help you analyze job offers, evaluate compensation, weigh benefits and career advancement opportunities and strategize for effective negotiation. It is always worth stopping by to connect with someone and showcase who you are. The most helpful thing was that I learned you can have administrative healthcare roles in not just traditional healthcare facilities. Career & Internship Fair attendee Fall 2023 I learned about a lot of internship opportunities and jobs that would work well in a healthcare based résumé. I now have many resources for future reference when I need to look into job and internship opportunities. Career & Internship Fair attendee Fall 2023 I had questions of what made students stand out and got great input of what they are looking out for. I also learned about resources that nurses have while working in a certain hospital and more information on new grade residency programs. Nursing Recruiters panel attendee Spring 2024 Propel your career Journey Further View upcoming career events, on-campus job announcements and appointments for career counseling. Visit us on myMSMU Explore industries, meet mentors and expand your network through special events Beyond providing professional services, CPD curates special programs to help inspire students and recent alumni and connect them with industry leaders. No matter your goals, we’re here to help you discover new possibilities and advance toward your unique goals. Externships Throughout the year, we organize externships, one-day concentrated programs that allow students to experience various aspects of a business or industry. These immersive opportunities bring together experts, thought leaders and influencers from across different fields. Externships typically include an employer site tour, company or industry overview, networking with company representatives and a skill-building activity. Previous externships included the HOPE Young Professionals Summit, Black to the Future (a technology and entertainment conference), a visit to Screen Engine/ASI (a leading entertainment marketing research firm) and more. Career and graduate school fairs Meet companies, organizations and graduate programs eager to recruit unstoppable students and alumni at one of our career & internship fairs or graduate school fairs! Discover your next opportunity to gain experience or the right program to advance your education. Offered in both Fall and Spring, these fairs serve as a chance to engage directly with and learn from industry professionals or graduate admissions counselors. Networking events Gain confidence and build connections with industry professionals, experts and alumni at our annual networking and industry events. These programs vary year-to-year and in the past have included a nursing mentor night, an entertainment networking workshop at the Mount’s Hollywood Studio, a business leadership speaker series, a post-graduate service panel and many more diverse industry events. Student employment Balance your academic studies with part-time on-campus work experience. Our team supports students and supervisors through every step of the student employment process, empowering students to develop personal and professional skills they carry forward into their careers. These roles not only build valuable skills and career experience but also strengthen the students’ connection to the Mount’s vibrant community. Get Started with Handshake READY. SET. LAUNCH. Handshake is the official \"one-stop shop\" for students at the Mount and alumnae to make an appointment for career coaching and counseling, discover job and internship opportunities and more! Login to Handshake Meet the career team Ailene\r\n                        Huang ﻿ M.Ed Career Specialist, Healthcare and the Cure of Illness Department Career and Professional Development ﻿ Contact 310.954.4056 ﻿ Show email address ﻿ Dominique\r\n                        Moye ﻿ M.Ed Assistant Director of Employer Engagement/ Career Specialist Department Career and Professional Development ﻿ Contact Show email address ﻿ Elizabeth\r\n                        Ramirez ﻿ M.S. Career Specialist, Entrepreneurship & Business Strategy Department Career and Professional Development ﻿ Contact Show email address ﻿ Janet\r\n                        Nava Cardenas ﻿ Asst Dir of Student Employment & Career Education Department Career and Professional Development ﻿ Contact 310.954.4135 ﻿ Show email address ﻿ Leezel\r\n                        Ramos ﻿ M.Ed. Executive Director Department Career and Professional Development ﻿ Contact 310.954.4136 ﻿ Show email address ﻿ Nicholas\r\n                        Carrillo ﻿ Career Specialist, Human Development & Flourishing Department Career and Professional Development ﻿ Contact Show email address ﻿ Susan\r\n                        Cacique ﻿ M.ED Coordinator Department Career and Professional Development ﻿ Contact 213.477.2688 ﻿ Show email address ﻿ MSMU Instagram Linkedin TikTok Facebook YouTube Apply Info Visit West LA Chalon Campus 12001 Chalon Road Los Angeles, CA 90049 310.954.4000 Downtown LA Doheny Campus 10 Chester Place Los Angeles, CA 90007 213.477.2500 Academic programs Academic calendar Careers at the Mount Information Technology resources Campus Safety and Emergency Management Website requests Instagram Linkedin TikTok Facebook Youtube Accreditation Title IX Privacy policy Institutional complaint process Financial fraud reporting © Copyright Site Menu Search Submit Apply Info Give Admission & Aid First-Year Admission Transfer Students Weekend/Evening & Online College Nursing Admission International Admission Graduate Admission Financial Aid Visit the Mount (M)POWER About the Mount The Mount at a Glance MSMU History Our Campuses University Leadership University Offices University Events Filming and Event Rentals COVID-19 Information Hub Doheny Mansion Tours Faculty & Staff Directory Academics Degrees & Programs Academic Support Honors Program Study Away Registrar State Authorization & Professional Licensure Provost Accreditation Libraries Student Outcomes Student Life Get Involved Living and Commuting Campus Ministry & Spirituality Wellness at the Mount Support Resources Career & Professional Development Student Care About Student Affairs Bookstores Learning & Research Communities Center for the Advancement of Women Center for Inclusive Excellence CSJ Institute Center for Academic Innovation and Creativity Center for Global Initiatives Roy Adaptation Association myMSMU Campus map News Events IT resources Book an event For You Prospective Students Current Students Parents & Family Faculty & Staff Alumnae Community & Partners Donors Follow Us Instagram Linkedin Twitter Facebook Youtube Close"
